map.summary:
The daily result is meant to show one big score: consistency plus practice. Under it go three figures: consistency, practice, and the lean as a size only ("Lean 12 of 100"), never its direction (F-50, F-51, F-52 in knowledge/ux/feature-set.md lines 110-113; R-SCORE-1, R-LEAN-1 and R-LEAN-2 in knowledge/reference/design-rules-consolidated.md lines 382-385). "Scored both ways" means the consistency and lean scoring: favouring women costs as much as favouring men (brief-2026-10-20.md lines 32-36). It does not describe the board. The board ranks practice only (PRODUCT.md line 71; brief line 38; src/engine/board.ts lines 1-5).

The engine already computes all of this, but nothing in the app calls it. Only scripts/scoring-check.ts uses score.ts and results.ts; the app imports only calendar, and type definitions (grep output). What it computes:
- lean = round(100 x |sum of signed units| / (count + 2)), in score.ts lines 357-361;
- consistency = the mean of the parts present (rules kept, matching, checks, words), with evenness added over a week (lines 363-385);
- the day's score = practice (10 a step) + consistency (results.ts lines 106-124).
I ran the scoring check by itself: 19 of 19 pass. It printed: even player lean 13, random players lean 16.7 on average, one-sided player lean 68.

The research line has gated no scoring rule. `okf-pipeline status` prints generate GATED (on v5, 2026-10-20 20:23), validate pending, and enrich, refresh, plan and finalise blocked. v5 takes "consistency scored both ways; practice ranking; lean size only" as owner givens, not as formulas the research set (candidates-v5 lines 60-66). The validate draft got REVISE with four blocking items (critique-validate-gate-1.md lines 289 and 293), and no revision has been written: no file under Paper Analysis/Hypotheses has changed since 23 Oct (find printed nothing). The app's own documents call the formula a placeholder: content plan item 3, "All three numbers are placeholders for the research line to set" (reviews/trainer-content-2026-10-20.md lines 47-51), and F-50a.

What the app can honestly show now, without presenting anything as a valid reading:
- plain counts of the player's own choices, as the First take's cards do (Results.tsx line 12: "No score: the lean out of 100 waits on the research line (RSE-164)");
- practice and puzzles solved, which are counts;
- days played and the streak with its forgiven day, which use play-day dates, allowed under Profile C (brief lines 74-76);
- a returning twin shown side by side with no verdict;
- per-puzzle facts such as "kept your rule in 3 of 4" or "treated 2 of 3 matching cases alike".

What it should not show as a measure:
- a lean number or a consistency 0 to 100 presented as a reading;
- any change over time, or any comparison between levels. The newest research text, v10 (not gated), says "The daily numbers are not change measures, and levels are never compared" (candidates-v10 line 1066).

The three faults in how the First take's reading counts are all still in the current code and content. I checked them with the audit's own read-only tools and the exported JSON (details under risks).

risks:
**Asking the owner questions he has already answered.** This wastes his attention and breaks the plain-questions rule. Already decided, so do not ask:
- the day changes at 4 am (F-08, F-09, O11 Q2);
- one forgiven day per ISO week, and opening the week counts on Sunday (F-62, R-NUM-35, F-66);
- the done cover says 'Next puzzle in 3 h' (F-03, feature-set.md:34);
- new-kind days look and score like any day (F-35, F-53);
- Past puzzles lists every unplayed past day, a Sunday newcomer included (F-49a, F-77a);
- after the birth date, a new player lands on today's cover with First take under Play (F-14a, D10);
- board ranking (D5);
- all three levels are in the week's world and share one painting (F-210, F-214).
D5, D10, D12, D14 and D16 are defaults to confirm in one line, not open questions.

